.SSS "Designating \(lqSoft\(rq (Down-Line Loadable) Character Sets"
It is possible for you to define a soft character set that may or may
not replace one of the existing \(lqhard\(rq sets (ROM based fonts). If
you do replace a \(lqhard\(rq set, the replacement occurs for both the
80 and 132 column version. A soft font which replaces a hard font
remains in effect until the soft font is cleared or redefined. The soft
font is cleared by RECALL, DEFAULT, self test, power up, and is
redefined by DECDLD. If the soft character set you define does not
replace an existing hard set, then it is used in addition to the hard
sets.
.P
.B NOTE:
.B Designation of a soft character set is supported only in the VT200
.B mode.
.P
